details:
(a) the details of central funds sanctioned for the proposed sports city in Ahmedabad, year-wise, since the project's inception;
(b) whether similar central funding has been extended to sports infrastructure projects in other cities preparing for major multi-sport events, including Commonwealth Games and Olympic bid preparations;
(c) if so, the city-wise details of funds released; and
(d) the criteria adopted by the Ministry in prioritising cities for such infrastructure grants?

(a) the details of proposals of Government of Tamil Nadu pending with the Ministry under Swadesh Darshan 2.0, PRASHAD and the Challenge-Based Destination Development Scheme, proposal-wise, with the date of submission, present status and reasons for pendency;
(b) the project-wise funds released and utilisation reported against projects sanctioned under these schemes; and
(c) whether any destination in the State has been selected for development under these schemes for iconic tourist centres and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether the National Disaster Management Authority's (NDMA's) guidelines on cyclone and flood preparedness have been implemented in Tamil Nadu's coastal districts, if so, the district-wise status thereof;
(b) the capacity-building, mock drills and preparedness exercises conducted jointly by the NDMA and Government of Tamil Nadu during the last two years, with district-wise details thereof; and
(c) whether any gap in disaster preparedness have been identified during such exercises or assessments, if so, the corrective measures taken?

(a) key methodological changes adopted in the new series of national accounts with base year 2022-23 released in February 2026, including the changes in data sources and deflation methods, as against the 2011-12 series;
(b) whether the States will follow the same methodology and base year for computing their Gross State Domestic Product (GSDP), if so, the guidance issued to the States and the timeline prescribed; and
(c) manner in which GSDP estimates will be computed and reconciled with the national estimates under the new base, and the technical assistance to be provided to the State Directorates of Economics and Statistics?

(a) whether the consent of all lower riparian basin States will be considered in determining the suitability of the Mekedatu Balancing Reservoir project;
(b) the impact of the project on presently uncontrolled catchment flows downstream of Krishnarajasagara and Kabini, the Shimsha, Arkavathy and Suvarnavathy sub-basins;
(c) the hydrological studies and methodology relied upon by the CWC, CWMA and CWRC while examining the project, particularly its impact on releases at Biligundlu;
(d) whether the assessment examined monthly release schedules, besides the annual allocation of 177.25 TMC; and
(e) the annual quantum of uncontrolled flows proposed to be impounded and whether it has been independently verified by CWC/CWMA?

(a) the central funds released so far for the PM MITRA Park at Virudhunagar against the approved outlay and the progress of trunk infrastructure;
(b) the status of the proposed 15 MLD Common Effluent Treatment Plant and 20 MLD Zero Liquid Discharge facilities;
(c) whether units can commence operations before these are functional;
(d) the land allotted, investment committed and employment generated so far against the projected two lakh jobs; and
(e) the PLI and other incentives extended to units in the park, including for technical textiles?

(a) the performance of Chennai Flood Warning System (C-FLOWS) developed by NCCR during the northeast monsoons of 2023 to 2025, including verification statistics for its ward-level inundation forecasts;
(b) the upgrades planned to C-FLOWS, including extension beyond the Greater Chennai Corporation area and integration of AI-based models;
(c) the accuracy of IMD's heavy and extremely heavy rainfall forecasts for the districts of Tamil Nadu during the last three years; and
(d) whether comparable urban flood warning systems are proposed for Madurai, Coimbatore, Thoothukudi and Tirunelveli, in view of recent floods in the southern districts?

(a) the number of Agniveers who will complete their four-year engagement during 2026 and the number the Ministry expects to seek absorption in the Central Armed Police Forces (CAPFs) and Assam Rifles (ARs);
(b) the number of vacancies currently unfilled in the CAPFs and Assam Rifles, force-wise, and the number expected to be notified during 2026-27; and
(c) the number of ex-Agniveers recruited into the CAPFs to date under the reservations announced for them?

(a) the current level and composition of forex reserves and the decline from the February 2026 peak of $728.5 billion, with principal reasons;
(b) RBI's gross monthly dollar sales since February 2026 and any estimated cost of intervention;
(c) the import cover and reserve-to-short-term-debt ratio against RBI's own adequacy benchmarks; and
(d) any assessment of the effect and savings from appeals since May 2026 urging citizens to conserve foreign exchange?

(a) the number of critical mineral blocks auctioned tranche-wise to date, separately indicating blocks successfully allotted, blocks annulled for want of adequate response and blocks where mining or exploration has actually commenced;
(b) the acquisitions made and expenditure incurred by Khanij Bidesh India Ltd (KABIL) abroad, including the expected timeline for production from the lithium blocks in Catamarca, Argentina;
(c) the import dependence ratio for lithium, cobalt, nickel and rare earth elements for the latest available year, in value and volume; and
(d) the amount released and utilised so far against the ?34,300 crore outlay of the National Critical Mineral Mission, component-wise?

(a) the number of Mega Food Parks and Agro-Processing Clusters approved and made operational in Tamil Nadu under the Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana to date;
(b) the sanctioned versus achieved processing/preservation capacity at each such facility in the State;
(c) the employment generated against projections; and
(d) whether any approved facility in Tamil Nadu remains non-operational, if so, the reasons therefor?

(a) the names, designations and represented organisations of members of the Investment Committee of the Technology Development Board (TDB) under RDI scheme;
(b) whether any company funded by TDB under RDI scheme has also received funding from any organisation represented on this Committee or TDB's Governing Board and if so, the names of such companies; and
(c) whether TDB has a conflict-of-interest policy for Investment Committee members and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the number of Indian fishermen, State-wise, arrested by Sri Lankan authorities and the number of fishing boats seized, year-wise since 2023;
(b) the number of fishermen and boats currently in Sri Lankan custody and the number of boats confiscated or disposed of by Sri Lankan courts during this period;
(c) the dates and outcomes of meetings of India-Sri Lanka Joint Working Group on Fisheries held since 2023 and the specific mechanisms agreed to prevent recurring arrests; and
(d) the compensation or livelihood assistance extended by the Central Government to families of detained fishermen and to owners of boats not returned?

(a) the year-wise funds approved and released under the National Health Mission (NHM) to Tamil Nadu over the last three financial years;
(b) the reasons for any gap between funds approved and funds actually released;
(c) whether any conditions linked to Central Scheme compliance have affected timely release;
(d) the mechanism, if any, for States to appeal delayed disbursal; and
(e) the steps proposed to streamline release timelines going forward?

(a) the funds sanctioned and released to the State of Tamil Nadu under AMRUT 2.0 and the Smart Cities Mission over the last three financial years;
(b) the utilisation rate of released funds; and
(c) the reasons for any gap between sanction and release for urban local bodies in the State?

(a) the reasons for Tamil Nadu receiving a wage increase of around 3 percent under the newly notified VB-G RAM-G Act, 2025, against increases exceeding 15 percent for several northern and north-eastern States;
(b) the outstanding MGNREGA wage dues to Tamil Nadu as of the latest available date; and
(c) whether Tamil Nadu's historically high MGNREGA performance was factored into the 16th Finance Commission-linked devolution formula used to determine the State's normative allocation under the new scheme?

(a) the number of farmers enrolled and claims settled under Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY) in Thanjavur, Tiruvarur and Nagapattinam districts in each of the previous three years;
(b) the average time taken between claim intimation and settlement in these districts over this period;
(c) whether any insurance dues remain pending from earlier crop seasons, if so, since which year; and
(d) whether any risk assessment has factored in potential water disruption to the delta region from the proposed Mekedatu project?
